    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "A Vaisala CL51 ceilometer, owned by the University of Canterbury, Christchurch, New Zealand, was deployed aboard all voyages aboard Aurora Australis during season 2015/16. The ceilometer provided vertical profiles of cloud backscatter, as well as cloud base height and ceilometer instrumental status information.\n\nOne netCDF file per hour \n\nResolution: 10m vertically x 6 seconds.\n\nTime period: 19 October 2015 \u2013 22 February 2016\n\nAll times in UT (Universal Time)\n\nData converted into netCDF files by Peter Kuma, University of Canterbury.",
